{
  "about": "Browse Backups from the menu bar (docs/adr/0059-backups.mdx, decision 10), in Spanish, the screen reader on, as a Mac's Time Machine menu opens Enter Time Machine: the run's one backup service, a real oxyos-backupd --development, backed the run's home up to a played disk, “Disco de copias”, before the run, and plan.txt was deleted since; the menu bar's item and Dropsea ask that same service. Allo (sample/EditingProbe.tsx) is open. A press on the item opens its menu, said by its title and its first line (the latest backup's disk); ↓ reaches Hacer copia de seguridad ahora, ↓ again Explorar copias de seguridad, each said once, and Return chooses it: the session opens dropsea://backups in Dropsea, whose window takes the keyboard with nothing of it focused, as every launched application's does. Its Browse Backups shows the home as the newest backup held it: Documents, notas.txt and plan.txt, each an item of the list, plan.txt said to be gone (Ya no está aquí), Restaurar disabled with nothing chosen; its count is said once it is known (OxyHQ/Dropsea#59: never “0 elementos” while it looks). Tab puts the keyboard on the sidebar's first place, the home, its ring around it, said once. At scale 1.25 (the ThinkPad's panel).",
